1
00:00:00,912 --> 00:00:05,178
Welcome, everyone, to today's special
meeting on biblical prophecy.

2
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:09,924
Our gathering today has a title, and the
title is "At the Appointed Time."

3
00:00:09,954 --> 00:00:10,821
You might ask,

4
00:00:10,851 --> 00:00:12,553
who could be so purposeful,

5
00:00:12,583 --> 00:00:14,412
so thoughtful and deliberate,

6
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:16,464
as to work by an appointed time?

7
00:00:16,494 --> 00:00:19,478
And what exactly is it all meant to
accomplish?

8
00:00:19,508 --> 00:00:23,390
Well, in just a little while, it will all
become clear to us.

9
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:28,199
In the recent war between Russia and
Ukraine, I once saw a scene like this.

10
00:00:28,229 --> 00:00:33,521
Someone had laid out a great many toys,
right there along the border of Romania
and

11
00:00:33,551 --> 00:00:34,034
Ukraine.

12
00:00:34,064 --> 00:00:35,317
What they were doing

13
00:00:35,347 --> 00:00:40,960
was making sure that the children fleeing
the war could each receive a toy of their
own.

14
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:45,064
It made me think of the saying: the flames
of war are merciless,

15
00:00:45,094 --> 00:00:47,821
yet here in this world there is still
love.

16
00:00:47,851 --> 00:00:51,668
And in fact, human beings are made in the
very image of God.

17
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:53,977
The Bible tells us that God is love.

18
00:00:54,007 --> 00:00:56,991
And my hope is that, through today's
gathering,

19
00:00:57,021 --> 00:00:59,363
everyone here would come to know God,

20
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:01,223
and to come to know His love.

21
00:01:01,253 --> 00:01:03,467
The Chinese people are very clever,

22
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:05,134
and the Chinese characters

23
00:01:05,164 --> 00:01:06,417
are full of meaning.

24
00:01:06,447 --> 00:01:10,457
Take the character for "God" — it actually
has two parts to it.

25
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:14,432
On one side is the
 radical 示, the "s
pirit" or "altar" 
radical,

26
00:01:14,462 --> 00:01:17,061
and on the other s
ide is the charact
er 申.

27
00:01:17,091 --> 00:01:18,793
Now the ancient fo
rm of 示 —

28
00:01:18,823 --> 00:01:21,743
if you look at the image here, you'll see
that

29
00:01:21,773 --> 00:01:25,718
the single top stroke represents the
firmament, the sky above,

30
00:01:25,748 --> 00:01:29,309
the two strokes represent what lies above
the firmament,

31
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:34,183
and the three vertical strokes represent
what shines down from the heavens —

32
00:01:34,213 --> 00:01:37,138
the light of the sun, the moon, and the
stars.

33
00:01:37,168 --> 00:01:37,597
And so,

34
00:01:37,627 --> 00:01:41,527
the people of old felt that the heavens
display their signs,

35
00:01:41,557 --> 00:01:43,689
and from that they could perceive

36
00:01:43,719 --> 00:01:45,458
the very meaning of Heaven.

37
00:01:45,488 --> 00:01:51,485
And the character 
申, in its ancient 
form, carries the 
sense of a pair of
 hands reaching ou
t,

38
00:01:51,515 --> 00:01:53,320
a pair of outstretched arms.

39
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:56,006
So how does the Bible itself describe God

40
00:01:56,036 --> 00:02:00,329
making this firmament? It records it like
this — what does it say?

41
00:02:00,359 --> 00:02:00,919
God said,

42
00:02:00,949 --> 00:02:04,326
"Let there be lights in the firmament of
the heavens

43
00:02:04,356 --> 00:02:06,488
to divide the day from the night;

44
00:02:06,518 --> 00:02:08,125
and let them be for signs

45
00:02:08,155 --> 00:02:09,174
and for seasons,

46
00:02:09,204 --> 00:02:09,960
and for days

47
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:10,877
and for years;

48
00:02:10,907 --> 00:02:14,677
and let them be for lights in the
firmament of the heavens

49
00:02:14,707 --> 00:02:16,642
to give light upon the earth";

50
00:02:16,672 --> 00:02:17,559
and it was so.

51
00:02:17,589 --> 00:02:19,590
Then God made two great lights:

52
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:24,438
the greater light to rule the day, and the
lesser light to rule the night.

53
00:02:24,468 --> 00:02:25,945
He made the stars also.

54
00:02:25,975 --> 00:02:27,255
God set these lights

55
00:02:27,285 --> 00:02:29,286
in the firmament of the heavens

56
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:31,186
to give light upon the earth,

57
00:02:31,216 --> 00:02:36,296
to rule over the day and the night, and to
divide the light from the darkness.

58
00:02:36,326 --> 00:02:37,016
And God saw

59
00:02:37,046 --> 00:02:38,130
that it was good.

60
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:40,096
I wonder whether you noticed —

61
00:02:40,126 --> 00:02:44,550
even in that short little passage, you can
already come to know God.

62
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:49,333
Just think about how God made the lights
of heaven. It says, "God said" —

63
00:02:49,363 --> 00:02:51,036
that is, God simply spoke,

64
00:02:51,066 --> 00:02:53,264
and then it says, "and it was so."

65
00:02:53,294 --> 00:02:56,277
It turns out that God is full of mighty
power:

66
00:02:56,307 --> 00:02:59,291
the very things He speaks simply come to
pass.

67
00:02:59,321 --> 00:03:02,435
So in English there's actually a word for
this —

68
00:03:02,465 --> 00:03:04,794
the word for the cosmos, "universe."

69
00:03:04,824 --> 00:03:07,414
"Universe" — "uni," or "uno," means one,

70
00:03:07,444 --> 00:03:10,370
and "verse" means a single utterance, a
word.

71
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,528
People held a concept of where the
universe came from:

72
00:03:13,558 --> 00:03:16,744
it came from one word of God, simply
spoken into being.

73
00:03:16,774 --> 00:03:20,604
And notice, too, at the very end — "and
God saw that it was good."

74
00:03:20,634 --> 00:03:23,235
I think God has a wonderful sense of
leisure;

75
00:03:23,265 --> 00:03:25,107
He isn't only ever busy at work.

76
00:03:25,137 --> 00:03:28,674
He is also able to stop and take delight
in what He has made.

77
00:03:28,704 --> 00:03:31,013
Today, God is the very One who made you,

78
00:03:31,043 --> 00:03:32,826
He understands you best of all,

79
00:03:32,856 --> 00:03:35,808
and He is the One most able to take
delight in you.

80
00:03:35,838 --> 00:03:37,562
Let me ask you all a question.

81
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:40,603
Which do you think is bigger — the moon,
or the sun?

82
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:41,480
You might think

83
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:43,761
this question is really far too silly —

84
00:03:43,791 --> 00:03:45,866
of course the sun is the bigger one.

85
00:03:45,896 --> 00:03:47,153
But the people of old,

86
00:03:47,183 --> 00:03:52,767
some of them would say the moon is bigger.
And why? Because sometimes, on a dark
night, when you

87
00:03:52,797 --> 00:03:57,445
look up at the moon, it looks enormous —
have you ever heard of the "supermoon"?

88
00:03:57,475 --> 00:04:01,480
Or when you climb up a mountain and see
the moon smiling down at you,

89
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:03,878
that is what we call the "moon illusion."

90
00:04:03,908 --> 00:04:07,679
And still others had an explanation like
this. What did they say?

91
00:04:07,709 --> 00:04:10,427
When you look up and the moon appears so
large,

92
00:04:10,457 --> 00:04:15,222
and the sun also appears about that large
— when the two seem about the same size,

93
00:04:15,252 --> 00:04:16,977
and yet the sun is so very hot

94
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:19,959
and the moon so very cold — just think, if
you were

95
00:04:19,989 --> 00:04:21,304
sitting beside a stove,

96
00:04:21,334 --> 00:04:25,748
the closer you are the hotter it is, and
the farther away the colder, right?

97
00:04:25,778 --> 00:04:30,602
So that would mean the moon is the one
near to us, and the sun is the one far off
—

98
00:04:30,632 --> 00:04:33,234
but since the two appear about the same
size,

99
00:04:33,264 --> 00:04:38,672
if the moon is farther and still looks
that big, that would prove the moon is the
bigger one.

100
00:04:38,702 --> 00:04:42,239
So in the old days, people would actually
argue it like that.

101
00:04:42,269 --> 00:04:47,359
But that passage from a moment ago — the
Bible has already given me the answer.

102
00:04:47,389 --> 00:04:51,182
God made the two great lights, the greater
to rule the day.

103
00:04:51,212 --> 00:04:52,183
In the daytime,

104
00:04:52,213 --> 00:04:53,518
when the sun is out,

105
00:04:53,548 --> 00:04:56,588
most of the time you can't even see the
moon —

106
00:04:56,618 --> 00:04:58,323
the greater rules the day,

107
00:04:58,353 --> 00:05:00,125
the lesser rules the night.

108
00:05:00,155 --> 00:05:02,652
Already, over three thousand years ago,

109
00:05:02,682 --> 00:05:05,633
this one passage of Scripture had already
told

110
00:05:05,663 --> 00:05:08,874
me that the sun is, in fact, bigger than
the moon.

111
00:05:08,904 --> 00:05:11,466
And moonlight is something very special.

112
00:05:11,496 --> 00:05:16,585
Its glow is bright and pure, and when the
moon is full it is very large indeed.

113
00:05:16,615 --> 00:05:18,659
I think it really is beautiful —

114
00:05:18,689 --> 00:05:20,538
like a great big street-lamp.

115
00:05:20,568 --> 00:05:26,176
Isn't moonlight romantic? And yet you
needn't ever worry about bumping into a
lamppost.

116
00:05:26,206 --> 00:05:27,732
Now if you look up high,

117
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:28,963
apart from the sun,

118
00:05:28,993 --> 00:05:29,870
and apart from

119
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:30,777
the full moon,

120
00:05:30,807 --> 00:05:33,564
what is the third brightest thing up
there?

121
00:05:33,594 --> 00:05:34,601
It isn't Sirius,

122
00:05:34,631 --> 00:05:39,656
and it isn't the North Star either — most
of the time, it is the planet Venus.

123
00:05:39,686 --> 00:05:44,905
This is what many people call the morning
star: just before daybreak, you can see

124
00:05:44,935 --> 00:05:47,173
one single, especially bright star.

125
00:05:47,203 --> 00:05:52,552
When you see the morning star, daybreak is
very near, and the sun is about to rise.

126
00:05:52,582 --> 00:05:54,172
And so, within the Bible,

127
00:05:54,202 --> 00:05:55,857
through this morning star,

128
00:05:55,887 --> 00:05:59,874
God reminds us and teaches us something.
Here is what it says:

129
00:05:59,904 --> 00:06:03,503
It says: we also have the prophetic word
made more sure,

130
00:06:03,533 --> 00:06:05,836
like a lamp shining in a dark place,

131
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:11,604
which you do well to heed, until the day
dawns and the morning star rises in your
hearts.

132
00:06:11,634 --> 00:06:13,613
The Bible uses the morning star

133
00:06:13,643 --> 00:06:15,039
to speak of prophecy —

134
00:06:15,069 --> 00:06:17,112
as if, together in the darkness,

135
00:06:17,142 --> 00:06:22,037
when you have no direction and no hope,
you catch sight of the morning star,

136
00:06:22,067 --> 00:06:28,977
and you know daybreak is near. In the same
way, prophecy lets me know that the words
of the Bible are true.

137
00:06:29,007 --> 00:06:30,457
God's promises are true.

138
00:06:30,487 --> 00:06:34,403
So many circumstances, so many troubles,
will one day pass away,

139
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:35,882
and God will bring hope.

140
00:06:35,912 --> 00:06:42,233
Speaking of prophecy, let me mention in
passing — some of the Bible's prophecies
have not yet happened,

141
00:06:42,263 --> 00:06:44,391
some are being fulfilled right now,

142
00:06:44,421 --> 00:06:47,288
but far more of them have already come to
pass.

143
00:06:47,318 --> 00:06:53,022
So the Bible has a saying: declare the
former things, what they were — that is,
to make clear

144
00:06:53,052 --> 00:06:55,550
what has happened, and how it came about,

145
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:57,831
so that we would know that the Bible,

146
00:06:57,861 --> 00:07:04,182
the word of God, is so accurate and so
remarkable. And tonight's gathering is for
exactly that purpose.

147
00:07:04,212 --> 00:07:10,224
And then, at the very end of the Bible,
the Lord Jesus Himself says: I am the
bright morning star.

148
00:07:10,254 --> 00:07:14,417
Look back at this world — think of how
severe the pandemic has been,

149
00:07:14,447 --> 00:07:16,205
and Europe once again at war.

150
00:07:16,235 --> 00:07:19,596
What on earth will become of the world
that lies ahead?

151
00:07:19,626 --> 00:07:21,322
But I find this so precious:

152
00:07:21,352 --> 00:07:24,343
the Lord says that He is the bright
morning star.

153
00:07:24,373 --> 00:07:26,809
He is the One who brings hope to people.

154
00:07:26,839 --> 00:07:30,817
And you'll notice, too, that when God made
the lights of heaven —

155
00:07:30,847 --> 00:07:31,125
wow —

156
00:07:31,155 --> 00:07:35,317
there was the sun, there was the moon, and
there were all the stars.

157
00:07:35,347 --> 00:07:38,955
And what were they for? They were to give
light in the sky,

158
00:07:38,985 --> 00:07:46,785
and to shine upon the earth. And this
phrase is mentioned twice — "to shine upon
the earth" — to let you know that all God
made

159
00:07:46,815 --> 00:07:48,142
was, in fact, for you.

160
00:07:48,172 --> 00:07:51,471
Such enormous heavenly bodies, all brought
into being,

161
00:07:51,501 --> 00:07:52,951
were made for your sake.

162
00:07:52,981 --> 00:07:53,937
So great a moon,

163
00:07:53,967 --> 00:07:58,870
so great a sun brought forth — it was for
you, to give its light upon the earth.

164
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:01,397
Doesn't it shine its light down upon you?

165
00:08:01,427 --> 00:08:05,413
These lights have a real purpose: to
divide the day from the night,

166
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:08,889
and to be for signs, for seasons, for
days, and for years.

167
00:08:08,919 --> 00:08:14,164
So God taught — that is, through the very
things He made, He taught the people of
Israel

168
00:08:14,194 --> 00:08:15,362
a great many things.

169
00:08:15,392 --> 00:08:19,258
And the very first of them is this: how is
a single day reckoned?

170
00:08:19,288 --> 00:08:20,817
It is that first there was

171
00:08:20,847 --> 00:08:21,536
the evening,

172
00:08:21,566 --> 00:08:24,772
and then the morning — and that is counted
as one day.

173
00:08:24,802 --> 00:08:27,769
So how does a Jewish day actually begin?
It begins

174
00:08:27,799 --> 00:08:32,924
from the sunset of one day, at dusk, and
runs all the way to the dusk of the next
day.

175
00:08:32,954 --> 00:08:37,539
And in this you can see that God greatly
desires that people would have rest.

176
00:08:37,569 --> 00:08:42,693
And then there is that word for "appointed
season" — it is a very special word
indeed.

177
00:08:42,723 --> 00:08:48,387
You'll find some Bibles translate it as
"seasons," but many others translate it as
"festivals,"

178
00:08:48,417 --> 00:08:50,185
or even as "special meetings."

179
00:08:50,215 --> 00:08:53,242
It turns out that the word for "appointed
season" —

180
00:08:53,272 --> 00:08:58,336
its original meaning, the sense of the
original language, is this: an appointed
date,

181
00:08:58,366 --> 00:08:59,535
an agreed-upon time.

182
00:08:59,565 --> 00:09:04,030
So to translate it as "festival" is very
meaningful too — it means that God

183
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:07,686
appoints a time with people and calls them
to keep the feast,

184
00:09:07,716 --> 00:09:13,080
appoints a time so that people would
return before Him and enjoy that shared
joy together.

185
00:09:13,110 --> 00:09:14,759
That is what it truly means.

186
00:09:14,789 --> 00:09:16,257
And so, within the Bible,

187
00:09:16,287 --> 00:09:19,853
God taught the people of Israel just how
to keep the feasts.

188
00:09:19,883 --> 00:09:26,566
And one of them is this — the very first
thing mentioned when God teaches people to
keep a feast is the Sabbath.

189
00:09:26,596 --> 00:09:31,900
And what does the Sabbath mean? It means
that for six days there is work you ought
to do,

190
00:09:31,930 --> 00:09:33,279
but on the seventh day,

191
00:09:33,309 --> 00:09:35,376
you lay down the work of your hands

192
00:09:35,406 --> 00:09:36,635
and you come to rest.

193
00:09:36,665 --> 00:09:38,090
So you can see that God

194
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:41,315
first gave people the evening and then the
morning,

195
00:09:41,345 --> 00:09:41,821
six days

196
00:09:41,851 --> 00:09:47,449
of labor, and then rest on the seventh.
From this you can see that God truly calls
people

197
00:09:47,479 --> 00:09:48,904
to have real enjoyment,

198
00:09:48,934 --> 00:09:51,939
that God truly calls people to enjoy their
rest.

199
00:09:51,969 --> 00:09:58,643
When the Lord Jesus came, He too said this
— He spoke of Himself in particular as the
Lord of the Sabbath.

200
00:09:58,673 --> 00:10:03,196
And what did He say? "Come to Me, all you
who labor and are heavy laden,

201
00:10:03,226 --> 00:10:03,892
come to Me,

202
00:10:03,922 --> 00:10:05,536
and I will give you rest."

203
00:10:05,566 --> 00:10:07,243
I wonder, in your own life,

204
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:13,378
in all that you have been through, whether
you ever feel that life lays so many
burdens upon you,

205
00:10:13,408 --> 00:10:15,591
that you are carrying a heavy load.

206
00:10:15,621 --> 00:10:19,955
In fact, when the Lord Jesus came, He is
well able to understand you.

207
00:10:19,985 --> 00:10:25,393
He is able to sympathize with you, and He
longs for you to set down your heavy
burden.

208
00:10:25,423 --> 00:10:27,543
He longs for you to come and rest.

209
00:10:27,573 --> 00:10:29,441
This is the very heart of God.

210
00:10:29,471 --> 00:10:31,591
So God called the people of Israel

211
00:10:31,621 --> 00:10:32,856
to keep the feasts —

212
00:10:32,886 --> 00:10:35,006
and there are seven feasts in all.

213
00:10:35,036 --> 00:10:37,282
We call them the Feasts of the LORD.

214
00:10:37,312 --> 00:10:41,266
And you'll find something fascinating
about these seven feasts:

215
00:10:41,296 --> 00:10:45,883
they seem to cluster at two times — you
could call them the autumn feasts

216
00:10:45,913 --> 00:10:47,274
and the spring feasts.

217
00:10:47,304 --> 00:10:50,057
Let me think — now that I'm here in
America,

218
00:10:50,087 --> 00:10:54,610
in many places, much of the time, there's
a holiday every single month —

219
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:57,456
every month there's a so-called long
weekend.

220
00:10:57,486 --> 00:11:00,934
Having a holiday every month is nice, but
you'll notice

221
00:11:00,964 --> 00:11:06,373
something fascinating: these seven feasts
are not scattered evenly across every
month.

222
00:11:06,403 --> 00:11:09,730
And you'll see there are three of them
marked in red.

223
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:10,466
The Sabbath

224
00:11:10,496 --> 00:11:18,291
is when you rest at home, laying down all
your work, to be at rest; but keeping
these feasts was something different.

225
00:11:18,321 --> 00:11:19,562
Three times a year,

226
00:11:19,592 --> 00:11:24,377
the people of Israel were to go up to
Jerusalem to keep the feast there,

227
00:11:24,407 --> 00:11:25,848
to go up to the temple

228
00:11:25,878 --> 00:11:27,855
and worship God in that place.

229
00:11:27,885 --> 00:11:32,670
And here is something fascinating too —
God called them up to Jerusalem,

230
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:36,884
and you'll see that all of these feasts
fall in the dry season.

231
00:11:36,914 --> 00:11:43,505
Not in the rainy season — for if they had
to go up to Jerusalem, traveling far, and
the rains came,

232
00:11:43,535 --> 00:11:45,712
everywhere would be mud and mire.

233
00:11:45,742 --> 00:11:48,454
But you'll find that God, for their sake,

234
00:11:48,484 --> 00:11:50,728
so that they could keep the feast,

235
00:11:50,758 --> 00:11:53,270
so that they could walk out His word —

236
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,945
you'll find that there was a dry season,

237
00:11:55,975 --> 00:11:58,687
and God's promise too: when they went up,

238
00:11:58,717 --> 00:12:05,242
no one would seize their fields or take
their property. On the contrary, when the
people of Israel

239
00:12:05,272 --> 00:12:09,923
kept the feast in this way, the whole land
was at peace on every side.

240
00:12:09,953 --> 00:12:11,863
But in fact, within the Bible

241
00:12:11,893 --> 00:12:14,137
there is a very important message:

242
00:12:14,167 --> 00:12:16,076
that God would send a Savior.

243
00:12:16,106 --> 00:12:19,153
And this Savior would come to the earth
twice.

244
00:12:19,183 --> 00:12:20,691
The Feasts of the LORD.

245
00:12:20,721 --> 00:12:24,236
It can also reveal God's own timetable,
His calendar.

246
00:12:24,266 --> 00:12:28,182
It can reveal the two comings of the
Savior whom God sends.

247
00:12:28,212 --> 00:12:33,466
We know that over two thousand years ago,
the Lord Jesus came and became a man,

248
00:12:33,496 --> 00:12:36,208
and for our sake was hung upon the cross.

249
00:12:36,238 --> 00:12:38,549
Then the Lord ascended into heaven,

250
00:12:38,579 --> 00:12:41,969
the Holy Spirit came down, and the church
appeared.

251
00:12:41,999 --> 00:12:43,245
And so we come, right up

252
00:12:43,275 --> 00:12:44,254
to the present day,

253
00:12:44,284 --> 00:12:49,729
and what you see is that the Lord will
keep His promise to come back and receive
the church to Himself.

254
00:12:49,759 --> 00:12:50,951
In heaven there will be

255
00:12:50,981 --> 00:12:55,469
the rewarding before the judgment seat of
Christ, and the marriage feast of the
Lamb,

256
00:12:55,499 --> 00:12:58,977
while on the earth there will be seven
years of great tribulation.

257
00:12:59,007 --> 00:13:03,069
And after those seven years, the Lord will
descend together with us. You see,

258
00:13:03,099 --> 00:13:05,726
this Savior comes to the earth two
separate times.

259
00:13:05,756 --> 00:13:09,181
And this, in fact, is one of the very
cores of biblical prophecy.

260
00:13:09,211 --> 00:13:10,138
As we were saying,

261
00:13:10,168 --> 00:13:11,413
these appointed feasts —

262
00:13:11,443 --> 00:13:15,612
these seven feasts — begin with the
Passover, which falls in their first
month,

263
00:13:15,642 --> 00:13:18,163
beginning on the fourteenth of that first
month.

264
00:13:18,193 --> 00:13:24,754
And then, following right behind it, comes
the Feast of Unleavened Bread. As we said,
you'll notice it runs from the 15th to

265
00:13:24,784 --> 00:13:25,232
the 21st.

266
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:27,836
The Feast of Unleavened Bread begins on
the 14th,

267
00:13:27,866 --> 00:13:30,547
at sunset — that is, around six o'clock,
it begins.

268
00:13:30,577 --> 00:13:35,330
The Passover is very special; in a little
while, when we come to it, you'll
understand it.

269
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:39,742
After the Passover, following right behind
it, comes the Feast of Unleavened Bread.

270
00:13:39,772 --> 00:13:44,897
But here's something fascinating — you'll
notice that the Feast of Firstfruits has
no fixed date,

271
00:13:44,927 --> 00:13:47,395
and Pentecost has no fixed date either,
because

272
00:13:47,425 --> 00:13:49,574
each and every year it falls differently.

273
00:13:49,604 --> 00:13:52,976
So how is the Feast of Firstfruits
reckoned? It is the day after

274
00:13:53,006 --> 00:13:55,048
the Sabbath that follows the Passover —

275
00:13:55,078 --> 00:13:56,802
that is the Feast of Firstfruits.

276
00:13:56,832 --> 00:14:00,842
And so you'll notice that between the
Feast of Firstfruits and the Passover,

277
00:14:00,872 --> 00:14:04,296
there may be just one day, or there may be
as many as seven days.

278
00:14:04,326 --> 00:14:08,973
It isn't fixed at all — it depends
entirely on when the Passover itself
happens to fall.

279
00:14:09,003 --> 00:14:12,215
So you'll find that the Feast of
Firstfruits has no set date:

280
00:14:12,245 --> 00:14:15,670
it is simply the day after the Sabbath
that follows the Passover.

281
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,682
And what, then, is Pentecost?

282
00:14:17,712 --> 00:14:21,013
It is, in fact, after the Feast of
Firstfruits —

283
00:14:21,043 --> 00:14:23,025
the day after seven Sabbaths,

284
00:14:23,055 --> 00:14:28,298
that is, seven sevens, which is
forty-nine, plus one more day, making
fifty.

285
00:14:28,328 --> 00:14:33,849
So "Pentecost" means this — "pente" is
fifty — fifty days later comes Pentecost.

286
00:14:33,879 --> 00:14:39,123
From this you can see that the first four
feasts are all connected together.

287
00:14:39,153 --> 00:14:41,343
It all begins with the Passover.

288
00:14:41,373 --> 00:14:44,466
In English the Passover is called
"Passover."

289
00:14:44,496 --> 00:14:46,963
You might find that rather curious —

290
00:14:46,993 --> 00:14:51,682
what does "pass over" mean? It means to
pass it by, to pass over it.

291
00:14:51,712 --> 00:14:54,527
So how was the Passover first instituted?

292
00:14:54,557 --> 00:15:00,980
It was back in the day when the people of
Israel were still slaves in Egypt. God
called Moses

293
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:05,975
to teach the people of Israel to keep the
feast — let me read it to you.

294
00:15:06,005 --> 00:15:10,416
It says: The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron
in the land of Egypt,

295
00:15:10,446 --> 00:15:11,249
telling them

296
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:13,955
to set this month as their first month,

297
00:15:13,985 --> 00:15:17,632
the beginning of months, the first month
of the year.

298
00:15:17,662 --> 00:15:23,600
It was the very day God would bring Israel
out of Egypt, so God said to set this
month

299
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:23,738
as

300
00:15:23,768 --> 00:15:25,542
the beginning of the year.

301
00:15:25,572 --> 00:15:28,873
And on the tenth of that month, the first
month,

302
00:15:28,903 --> 00:15:32,897
every household, every father's house, was
to take a lamb,

303
00:15:32,927 --> 00:15:34,840
one lamb for each household.

304
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:38,101
And this lamb had to meet certain
requirements.

305
00:15:38,131 --> 00:15:40,114
It had to be without defect —

306
00:15:40,144 --> 00:15:42,958
not lame, not sick, a strong one-year-old

307
00:15:42,988 --> 00:15:43,375
male —

308
00:15:43,405 --> 00:15:47,057
a sheep would do, or a goat, but it had to
be a male.

309
00:15:47,087 --> 00:15:49,107
After it was chosen on the tenth,

310
00:15:49,137 --> 00:15:51,033
right up until the fourteenth —

311
00:15:51,063 --> 00:15:54,760
and why so strange? The 11th, the 12th,
the 13th, the 14th —

312
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:59,792
what were those days for? The household
had a purpose: to watch whether this lamb

313
00:15:59,822 --> 00:16:02,836
met the requirements — would it walk with
a limp,

314
00:16:02,866 --> 00:16:05,383
or lie there all day long without moving?

315
00:16:05,413 --> 00:16:10,167
They watched to see whether the lamb truly
met the conditions just mentioned.

316
00:16:10,197 --> 00:16:12,962
And when everything was found to be in
order,

317
00:16:12,992 --> 00:16:19,733
then at the twilight of the 14th of the
first month — and when is twilight? It is
from three o'clock to six —

318
00:16:19,763 --> 00:16:22,343
the people of Israel would kill this lamb.

319
00:16:22,373 --> 00:16:24,765
So the Passover is very special indeed.

320
00:16:24,795 --> 00:16:32,344
You'd say the Passover is the 14th of the
first month — yes, but in fact it is the
twilight of the 14th, only a few hours.

321
00:16:32,374 --> 00:16:36,258
The Passover is the 14th of the first
month, from three o'clock

322
00:16:36,288 --> 00:16:40,234
to six, the few hours of twilight — this
was the appointed time.

323
00:16:40,264 --> 00:16:43,961
After the lamb was killed that day, what
was done? Its blood

324
00:16:43,991 --> 00:16:46,508
was brushed onto the lintel of the house,

325
00:16:46,538 --> 00:16:48,185
and onto the two doorposts,

326
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:50,732
and the whole lamb was roasted with fire.

327
00:16:50,762 --> 00:16:52,161
It could not be boiled.

328
00:16:52,191 --> 00:16:54,646
It could not be prepared any other way —

329
00:16:54,676 --> 00:16:58,871
however else you might cook it, no; the
whole was roasted with fire.

330
00:16:58,901 --> 00:16:59,367
And then

331
00:16:59,397 --> 00:17:03,157
it was eaten together with unleavened
bread and bitter herbs.

332
00:17:03,187 --> 00:17:05,890
But in fact, all of this is a
foreshadowing.

333
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:10,425
And what does it foreshadow? It
foreshadows that God would send a Savior.

334
00:17:10,455 --> 00:17:13,531
And this Savior would be just like this
very lamb.

335
00:17:13,561 --> 00:17:18,191
We know the Lord was crucified — was He
not crowned with a crown of thorns,

336
00:17:18,221 --> 00:17:21,856
shedding His blood, His two hands nailed
fast to the cross?

337
00:17:21,886 --> 00:17:25,939
So the blood was brushed on the lintel,
and on the two doorposts.

338
00:17:25,969 --> 00:17:26,819
You might ask,

339
00:17:26,849 --> 00:17:33,290
why was no blood put on the threshold
below? This points to exactly this — that
the Lord was lifted up,

340
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:35,237
His feet lifted off the ground.

341
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:41,205
And of course there is a meaning here too:
the Lord's blood should never be trampled
underfoot.

342
00:17:41,235 --> 00:17:45,226
The whole lamb was roasted with fire,
enduring all of its agony.

343
00:17:45,256 --> 00:17:49,184
So you see what the focus of the Passover
is: it is that lamb —

344
00:17:49,214 --> 00:17:50,566
chosen from the tenth,

345
00:17:50,596 --> 00:17:51,194
set apart,

346
00:17:51,224 --> 00:17:53,079
and then, over those few days,

347
00:17:53,109 --> 00:17:54,524
verified and observed —

348
00:17:54,554 --> 00:17:55,906
was it without defect,

349
00:17:55,936 --> 00:17:57,414
was it strong and sound?

350
00:17:57,444 --> 00:17:59,801
And then, at the twilight of the 14th,

351
00:17:59,831 --> 00:18:00,681
it was killed,

352
00:18:00,711 --> 00:18:03,822
its blood brushed on the lintel and the
doorposts,

353
00:18:03,852 --> 00:18:05,204
and then it was eaten.

354
00:18:05,234 --> 00:18:11,549
The lamb, the whole lamb, was roasted. To
this very day the people of Israel still
keep the Passover.

355
00:18:11,579 --> 00:18:15,884
So at the Passover meal there are bitter
herbs, and unleavened bread,

356
00:18:15,914 --> 00:18:20,282
and one special thing too: a shank bone of
the lamb, the lamb's "arm."

357
00:18:20,312 --> 00:18:25,119
It has meaning too; in a little while,
when we come to it, you'll understand.

358
00:18:25,149 --> 00:18:28,511
So for all of these many years they kept
the Passover,

359
00:18:28,541 --> 00:18:30,836
always observing it in this very way,

360
00:18:30,866 --> 00:18:32,532
until one particular year —

361
00:18:32,562 --> 00:18:33,789
a very special year.

362
00:18:33,819 --> 00:18:37,621
For in the Bible there is the prophecy of
the seventy sevens.

363
00:18:37,651 --> 00:18:42,207
It was the prophet Daniel, grieved to the
heart that the people of Israel

364
00:18:42,237 --> 00:18:45,348
were constantly sinning and turning away
from God,

365
00:18:45,378 --> 00:18:47,484
to the point of the nation's ruin.

366
00:18:47,514 --> 00:18:50,939
He made intercession on behalf of the
people of Israel.

367
00:18:50,969 --> 00:18:54,961
And it turns out that when he prayed in
this way, God responded.

368
00:18:54,991 --> 00:18:57,281
I believe God's heart was deeply moved.

369
00:18:57,311 --> 00:18:59,720
And today, too, God is deeply responsive.

370
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:05,907
Just as today, when you see so many people
who are sick, or caught in the flames of
war — God is in fact

371
00:19:05,937 --> 00:19:08,763
full of compassion, and He is deeply
responsive.

372
00:19:08,793 --> 00:19:11,559
So God gave the prophecy of the seventy
sevens,

373
00:19:11,589 --> 00:19:13,462
revealing it to this man Daniel.

374
00:19:13,492 --> 00:19:21,374
And how does it read? "Seventy weeks are
determined for your people" — that is
Israel — "and for your holy city" — that
is Jerusalem.

375
00:19:21,404 --> 00:19:22,386
It has a purpose:

376
00:19:22,416 --> 00:19:24,051
to finish the transgression,

377
00:19:24,081 --> 00:19:25,420
to make an end of sins,

378
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:27,561
to make reconciliation for iniquity,

379
00:19:27,591 --> 00:19:33,451
to bring in everlasting righteousness, to
seal up vision and prophecy, and to anoint
the Most Holy.

380
00:19:33,481 --> 00:19:36,425
Now here there are, in fact, two sets of
purposes.

381
00:19:36,455 --> 00:19:38,269
The first is to deal with sin —

382
00:19:38,299 --> 00:19:41,006
"to finish the transgression" is God's
promise

383
00:19:41,036 --> 00:19:43,980
to give them power so that they would sin
no more,

384
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:48,264
and even "to make an end of sins" means
that He would deal with all sin,

385
00:19:48,294 --> 00:19:49,691
every last trace of sin.

386
00:19:49,721 --> 00:19:51,654
He would do away with sin itself.

387
00:19:51,684 --> 00:19:56,235
"To make reconciliation for iniquity"
means that all the consequences of sin,

388
00:19:56,265 --> 00:19:59,269
every price, He would repay, and clear it
all away.

389
00:19:59,299 --> 00:20:02,363
Simply put: to deal with sin completely
and utterly.

390
00:20:02,393 --> 00:20:05,575
"To bring in everlasting righteousness" —
to bring in,

391
00:20:05,605 --> 00:20:08,073
or to manifest, everlasting righteousness.

392
00:20:08,103 --> 00:20:14,201
"To seal up vision and prophecy" — now in
what situation do you seal something up?
When it is finished.

393
00:20:14,231 --> 00:20:20,388
When a particular case is finished, when
the file is complete, then you seal it. So
in fact, "to seal up

394
00:20:20,418 --> 00:20:25,087
vision and prophecy" means, simply put, to
fulfill the vision and the prophecy,

395
00:20:25,117 --> 00:20:26,872
"and to anoint the Most Holy."

396
00:20:26,902 --> 00:20:33,327
Now this prophecy of the seventy sevens —
we mentioned it in one of our earlier
special meetings, so I

397
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:38,895
would encourage you, when you have the
chance, to go back and watch it again, all
right?

398
00:20:38,925 --> 00:20:44,084
It was the meeting of March 19th; you can
find it on the church's YouTube channel.

399
00:20:44,114 --> 00:20:46,425
This prophecy of the seventy sevens —

400
00:20:46,455 --> 00:20:51,108
we'll present it here visually; the
pictures you see show this same thing:

401
00:20:51,138 --> 00:20:52,943
that it emphasizes two times,

402
00:20:52,973 --> 00:20:54,335
namely the two comings

403
00:20:54,365 --> 00:20:57,182
of this Savior. At His first coming, He
would

404
00:20:57,212 --> 00:20:58,764
finish the transgression,

405
00:20:58,794 --> 00:21:00,030
make an end of sins,

406
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,435
and make reconciliation for iniquity —

407
00:21:02,465 --> 00:21:03,890
He would deal with sin.

408
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:08,066
At His second coming, He would bring in
everlasting righteousness,

409
00:21:08,096 --> 00:21:10,218
fulfill every vision and prophecy,

410
00:21:10,248 --> 00:21:11,800
and anoint the Most Holy.

411
00:21:11,830 --> 00:21:13,129
So do you see it now?

412
00:21:13,159 --> 00:21:18,254
Because the Savior comes two times, this
is a central focus of biblical prophecy.

413
00:21:18,284 --> 00:21:19,330
And so this time,

414
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:26,797
we won't go into the whole of the seventy
sevens in detail, as I said at the start;
you can listen back to the earlier

415
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:31,416
special meeting. But I want you to notice
a few things. What does it say?

416
00:21:31,446 --> 00:21:35,529
"Seventy weeks are determined — so know
this, and understand it —

417
00:21:35,559 --> 00:21:41,414
from the going forth of the command to
restore and build Jerusalem, until Messiah
the Prince,

418
00:21:41,444 --> 00:21:44,578
there shall be seven sevens and sixty-two
sevens."

419
00:21:44,608 --> 00:21:50,273
It says that even in troublesome times,
Jerusalem, both street and wall, shall be
rebuilt.

420
00:21:50,303 --> 00:21:52,298
"And after the sixty-two sevens,

421
00:21:52,328 --> 00:21:55,525
Messiah shall be cut off, and shall have
nothing" —

422
00:21:55,555 --> 00:22:00,144
"and shall have nothing" — beyond the
plain sense of having nothing left,

423
00:22:00,174 --> 00:22:02,486
it in fact also carries this meaning:

424
00:22:02,516 --> 00:22:03,634
"not for Himself."

425
00:22:03,664 --> 00:22:05,726
That is, He would be cut off

426
00:22:05,756 --> 00:22:07,893
not for any cause of His own.

427
00:22:07,923 --> 00:22:11,330
All right, so it speaks of Messiah the
Prince.

428
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:12,525
Now it turns out

429
00:22:12,555 --> 00:22:14,956
that among the people of Israel,

430
00:22:14,986 --> 00:22:18,907
there were three kinds of people who were
anointed —

431
00:22:18,937 --> 00:22:21,566
meaning that at their inauguration,

432
00:22:21,596 --> 00:22:25,003
anointing oil would be poured upon their
head.

433
00:22:25,033 --> 00:22:28,067
And which three kinds of people? They are

434
00:22:28,097 --> 00:22:30,906
the king, the priest, and the prophet.

435
00:22:30,936 --> 00:22:34,194
Upon them the anointing oil would be
poured.

436
00:22:34,224 --> 00:22:36,286
And what else does this say?

437
00:22:36,316 --> 00:22:36,897
It says:

438
00:22:36,927 --> 00:22:42,011
from the going forth of the command to
restore and build Jerusalem,

439
00:22:42,041 --> 00:22:44,530
until Messiah the Prince appears,

440
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:46,896
there shall be seven sevens and

441
00:22:46,926 --> 00:22:48,166
sixty-two sevens.

442
00:22:48,196 --> 00:22:50,333
This picture shows it to you.

443
00:22:50,363 --> 00:22:51,304
Seven weeks —

444
00:22:51,334 --> 00:22:56,908
after these forty-nine years, Jerusalem,
both street and wall, was rebuilt.

445
00:22:56,938 --> 00:23:04,529
And after a further sixty-two sevens,
making sixty-nine sevens in all — and this
comes to four hundred

446
00:23:04,559 --> 00:23:06,248
and eighty-three years.

447
00:23:06,278 --> 00:23:11,104
After these 483 years had passed, that
Anointed One would appear.

448
00:23:11,134 --> 00:23:11,851
The Jewish

449
00:23:11,881 --> 00:23:17,530
calendar works like this: their year is
360 days, and so 483 years, in fact,

450
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:19,323
amounts to 173,880 days.

451
00:23:19,353 --> 00:23:22,461
Now the solar year that we speak of today,

452
00:23:22,491 --> 00:23:23,881
the solar calendar,

453
00:23:23,911 --> 00:23:25,375
is in fact 365 days,

454
00:23:25,405 --> 00:23:27,243
and about a quarter more.

455
00:23:27,273 --> 00:23:33,295
After careful study, when was this command
to restore and build Jerusalem issued?

456
00:23:33,325 --> 00:23:34,267
At that time,

457
00:23:34,297 --> 00:23:40,095
Persia had an emperor who issued the
command to build Jerusalem, and it was in

458
00:23:40,125 --> 00:23:42,194
444 BC, on the 5th of March.

459
00:23:42,224 --> 00:23:44,560
Starting from that very day,

460
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:45,658
if you add on

461
00:23:45,688 --> 00:23:46,756
173,880 days,

462
00:23:46,786 --> 00:23:47,601
you arrive

463
00:23:47,631 --> 00:23:48,362
at AD 33,

464
00:23:48,392 --> 00:23:50,136
on the 30th of March.

465
00:23:50,166 --> 00:23:53,515
And what was happening on that very day?

466
00:23:53,545 --> 00:23:57,064
On that day, it turns out, the Lord Jesus,

467
00:23:57,094 --> 00:23:59,261
in the identity of a King,

468
00:23:59,291 --> 00:24:01,204
entered into Jerusalem,

469
00:24:01,234 --> 00:24:03,823
on the last leg of His journey.

470
00:24:03,853 --> 00:24:06,695
At that time He told His disciples

471
00:24:06,725 --> 00:24:08,216
to untie a donkey,

472
00:24:08,246 --> 00:24:10,244
and He rode up upon it —

473
00:24:10,274 --> 00:24:13,454
the colt of a donkey, a little donkey.

474
00:24:13,484 --> 00:24:16,750
And the crowds lining the road cheered,

475
00:24:16,780 --> 00:24:20,298
welcoming Him, treating Him as their King.

476
00:24:20,328 --> 00:24:23,678
And this, it turns out, bore witness to,

477
00:24:23,708 --> 00:24:27,479
and fulfilled, this very saying of the
Bible,

478
00:24:27,509 --> 00:24:30,352
in the book of Zechariah, 500 BC —

479
00:24:30,382 --> 00:24:33,478
500 years before the Lord Jesus came,

480
00:24:33,508 --> 00:24:35,337
there was this saying:

481
00:24:35,367 --> 00:24:38,463
"Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion!

482
00:24:38,493 --> 00:24:41,082
Shout, O daughter of Jerusalem!

483
00:24:41,112 --> 00:24:44,039
Behold, your King is coming to you;

484
00:24:44,069 --> 00:24:47,250
He is just and endowed with salvation,

485
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,784
lowly, and riding on a donkey,

486
00:24:49,814 --> 00:24:52,319
a colt, the foal of a donkey."

487
00:24:52,349 --> 00:24:54,583
And indeed the Lord Jesus,

488
00:24:54,613 --> 00:24:56,847
riding on a donkey's colt,

489
00:24:56,877 --> 00:24:58,414
entered Jerusalem,

490
00:24:58,444 --> 00:25:00,852
fulfilling this very saying,

491
00:25:00,882 --> 00:25:02,288
and showing what?

492
00:25:02,318 --> 00:25:07,273
That He is the King who was to come — He
is that very King.

493
00:25:07,303 --> 00:25:10,315
People have carefully researched it,

494
00:25:10,345 --> 00:25:13,779
and as I said a moment ago, that very day

495
00:25:13,809 --> 00:25:14,877
was precisely

496
00:25:14,907 --> 00:25:16,398
the 30th of March,

497
00:25:16,428 --> 00:25:16,914
AD 33.

498
00:25:16,944 --> 00:25:19,426
So you find that from the command to

499
00:25:19,456 --> 00:25:23,473
rebuild Jerusalem until the appearing of
the Anointed One,

500
00:25:23,503 --> 00:25:29,754
the Lord's riding into Jerusalem on a
donkey, it was precisely sixty-nine sevens
of years.

501
00:25:29,784 --> 00:25:31,847
But that day was very special.

502
00:25:31,877 --> 00:25:34,080
That day was also, in that year,

503
00:25:34,110 --> 00:25:37,709
the tenth of the first month on the Jewish
calendar.

504
00:25:37,739 --> 00:25:39,383
And what does that mean?

505
00:25:39,413 --> 00:25:43,361
It was the very day the Passover lamb was
to be selected.

506
00:25:43,391 --> 00:25:50,199
So the Lord Jesus riding into Jerusalem on
a donkey also showed what He is: He is the
Lamb of God.

507
00:25:50,229 --> 00:25:53,270
So you find that after He entered
Jerusalem,

508
00:25:53,300 --> 00:25:54,874
He did not die at once.

509
00:25:54,904 --> 00:25:57,805
There were several days, and in those days

510
00:25:57,835 --> 00:26:02,829
He was verified to be that perfect Son of
Man, the spotless Lamb of God.

511
00:26:02,859 --> 00:26:07,295
And when it came to the twilight of the
14th of the first month,

512
00:26:07,325 --> 00:26:08,272
the Lord died.

513
00:26:08,302 --> 00:26:12,738
Upon the cross, He committed His spirit
into His Father's hands.

514
00:26:12,768 --> 00:26:13,645
And this also

515
00:26:13,675 --> 00:26:19,437
fulfilled the latter part of the seventy
sevens: "and after the sixty-two sevens" —

516
00:26:19,467 --> 00:26:21,112
after the 30th of March,

517
00:26:21,142 --> 00:26:21,810
afterward,

518
00:26:21,840 --> 00:26:25,089
a few days later, the Anointed One was cut
off.

519
00:26:25,119 --> 00:26:27,741
The Lord Jesus was hung upon the tree,

520
00:26:27,771 --> 00:26:31,998
having nothing. And it turns out that the
Lord, in His dying,

521
00:26:32,028 --> 00:26:35,766
did not die for Himself, not for any cause
of His own.

522
00:26:35,796 --> 00:26:40,195
So you'll find that the Bible gives no
small space to recording

523
00:26:40,225 --> 00:26:45,326
what happened in those few days after the
Lord Jesus rode into Jerusalem.

524
00:26:45,356 --> 00:26:47,768
And what happened in those few days

525
00:26:47,798 --> 00:26:54,194
was, in fact, to let us know that He is
the Lamb of God, that He is the One
without blemish.

526
00:26:54,224 --> 00:26:56,028
Let me give you an example.

527
00:26:56,058 --> 00:26:57,590
There was an occasion —

528
00:26:57,620 --> 00:26:59,220
that day was, I believe,

529
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:00,103
a Wednesday —

530
00:27:00,133 --> 00:27:03,227
when some people came and questioned the
Lord.

531
00:27:03,257 --> 00:27:07,710
Here it tells of a spy; as it says just
before, they wanted to get

532
00:27:07,740 --> 00:27:14,773
some handle against Him by testing Him, to
catch something in the Lord's words with
which to attack Him.

533
00:27:14,803 --> 00:27:18,305
So some spies questioned the Lord, saying,
"Teacher,

534
00:27:18,335 --> 00:27:21,361
we know that what You say and teach is
right,

535
00:27:21,391 --> 00:27:22,652
and that You do not

536
00:27:22,682 --> 00:27:24,350
show personal favoritism,

537
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:26,659
but teach the way of God in truth.

538
00:27:26,689 --> 00:27:30,191
Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to
Caesar, or not?"

539
00:27:30,221 --> 00:27:31,413
You'd think, well,

540
00:27:31,443 --> 00:27:33,247
that sounds rather sincere.

541
00:27:33,277 --> 00:27:37,933
But let me tell you — that opening was not
praise of the Lord at all.

542
00:27:37,963 --> 00:27:42,144
In fact, they were cutting off the Lord's
every way of escape.

543
00:27:42,174 --> 00:27:44,793
Because, you see, before this incident,

544
00:27:44,823 --> 00:27:46,355
some people had already

545
00:27:46,385 --> 00:27:48,868
challenged the Lord, questioning Him.

546
00:27:48,898 --> 00:27:51,381
They said, when You entered Jerusalem

547
00:27:51,411 --> 00:27:52,943
and went to the temple,

548
00:27:52,973 --> 00:27:58,784
and cleansed the temple, overturning those
who sold cattle and sheep — they asked
Him,

549
00:27:58,814 --> 00:28:04,082
"By what authority do You do these
things?" And the Lord asked them in
return,

550
00:28:04,112 --> 00:28:09,040
"The baptism of John — by what authority
was it; from where did it come?"

551
00:28:09,070 --> 00:28:11,960
And those people reasoned among
themselves.

552
00:28:11,990 --> 00:28:16,986
They thought, if we say John's baptism was
from heaven, the Lord will say,

553
00:28:17,016 --> 00:28:19,363
"Why then did you not believe him?"

554
00:28:19,393 --> 00:28:21,333
"Why did you not believe him?

555
00:28:21,363 --> 00:28:26,766
You believe John was from God — why then
do you not believe that I am from God?"

556
00:28:26,796 --> 00:28:32,268
But if they said John's baptism was of
men, not from God, they feared the people,

557
00:28:32,298 --> 00:28:35,058
for the people held John to be a prophet.

558
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:39,411
So they said to the Lord, "We do not
know," and would not answer.

559
00:28:39,441 --> 00:28:45,841
So you see that these spies were not
praising the Lord at all; they were
cutting off His escape.

560
00:28:45,871 --> 00:28:46,526
They said,

561
00:28:46,556 --> 00:28:48,374
"We know that You are true,

562
00:28:48,404 --> 00:28:50,359
that what You teach is right,

563
00:28:50,389 --> 00:28:55,083
that You show no partiality and do not
regard the appearance of men."

564
00:28:55,113 --> 00:29:00,106
And then they asked their question — it
was just one question, very simple:

565
00:29:00,136 --> 00:29:00,843
they asked,

566
00:29:00,873 --> 00:29:03,924
"Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar, or
not?"

567
00:29:03,954 --> 00:29:06,335
It really is that simple a question.

568
00:29:06,365 --> 00:29:11,224
But do not underestimate it — this
question is not at all easy to answer,

569
00:29:11,254 --> 00:29:16,113
because whichever way you answer, you run
into trouble; you are finished.

570
00:29:16,143 --> 00:29:17,185
And why is that?

571
00:29:17,215 --> 00:29:18,390
Because if you say

572
00:29:18,420 --> 00:29:20,600
one ought to pay taxes to Caesar,

573
00:29:20,630 --> 00:29:22,342
then those Jews would say,

574
00:29:22,372 --> 00:29:26,092
"You are surely a traitor" — that is,
you're encouraging

575
00:29:26,122 --> 00:29:32,120
the Romans to rule over the Jews, since
you would have the Jews pay their taxes to
Caesar.

576
00:29:32,150 --> 00:29:33,928
Wouldn't that then make you

577
00:29:33,958 --> 00:29:36,138
a Jewish traitor, a collaborator?

578
00:29:36,168 --> 00:29:44,108
But if the Lord said not to pay taxes to
Caesar, those others would say He was
inciting rebellion, stirring up the Jews

579
00:29:44,138 --> 00:29:45,514
to resist the Romans.

580
00:29:45,544 --> 00:29:48,193
So do you see how hard this question is?

581
00:29:48,223 --> 00:29:50,939
But how did the Lord answer it? He said —

582
00:29:50,969 --> 00:29:55,226
the Lord saw through their trickery, and
said, "Bring Me a coin.

583
00:29:55,256 --> 00:29:57,704
Whose image and inscription is this?"

584
00:29:57,734 --> 00:29:59,713
Those people said, "Caesar's."

585
00:29:59,743 --> 00:30:01,789
On the coin was Caesar's image.

586
00:30:01,819 --> 00:30:06,343
Then the Lord said, "The things that are
Caesar's, render to Caesar;

587
00:30:06,373 --> 00:30:07,214
and likewise,

588
00:30:07,244 --> 00:30:10,034
the things that are God's, render to God."

589
00:30:10,064 --> 00:30:12,190
What a fine answer that was.

590
00:30:12,220 --> 00:30:16,887
And what was the reaction of the people
there? They marveled.

591
00:30:16,917 --> 00:30:17,503
That is,

592
00:30:17,533 --> 00:30:19,505
His answer, His response —

593
00:30:19,535 --> 00:30:25,280
true to form, His answer gave them no
handle with which to accuse the Lord.

594
00:30:25,310 --> 00:30:33,133
They fell silent, unable to speak. And so,
from this, you can see that what happened
in those few days

595
00:30:33,163 --> 00:30:35,058
proved the Lord's wisdom,

596
00:30:35,088 --> 00:30:36,290
His perfection —

597
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:39,601
that He is indeed the spotless Lamb of
God.

598
00:30:39,631 --> 00:30:41,186
So a few days later,

599
00:30:41,216 --> 00:30:44,197
when the Lord was nailed to the cross,

600
00:30:44,227 --> 00:30:46,654
He did not die in some muddled,

601
00:30:46,684 --> 00:30:47,763
senseless way.

602
00:30:47,793 --> 00:30:54,847
Looking at this matter of the cross, you
come to know that the Lord is truly full
of wisdom.

603
00:30:54,877 --> 00:30:56,079
Our topic today,

604
00:30:56,109 --> 00:30:57,927
"At the Appointed Time,"

605
00:30:57,957 --> 00:31:00,390
is in fact a verse of Scripture.

606
00:31:00,420 --> 00:31:03,085
In the book of Romans it says this.

607
00:31:03,115 --> 00:31:06,858
It says: for when we were still without
strength,

608
00:31:06,888 --> 00:31:07,397
Christ,

609
00:31:07,427 --> 00:31:09,091
at the appointed time,

610
00:31:09,121 --> 00:31:10,400
died for sinners.

611
00:31:10,430 --> 00:31:13,249
It turns out that this appointed time

612
00:31:13,279 --> 00:31:14,404
was set by God.

613
00:31:14,434 --> 00:31:18,254
It was set for His Son, for the Lord Jesus
Christ.

614
00:31:18,284 --> 00:31:22,027
It was the Lord Jesus who, at the
appointed time,

615
00:31:22,057 --> 00:31:23,336
died for sinners.

616
00:31:23,366 --> 00:31:27,263
It says: scarcely for a righteous man will
one die;

617
00:31:27,293 --> 00:31:31,498
yet for a good man, perhaps one would even
dare to die.

618
00:31:31,528 --> 00:31:32,422
But Christ —

619
00:31:32,452 --> 00:31:34,577
while we were still sinners,

620
00:31:34,607 --> 00:31:35,501
died for us.

621
00:31:35,531 --> 00:31:36,656
The love of God

622
00:31:36,686 --> 00:31:37,811
is, right here,

623
00:31:37,841 --> 00:31:39,043
shown toward us.

624
00:31:39,073 --> 00:31:41,199
Sin is committed by people —

625
00:31:41,229 --> 00:31:44,754
each who sins bears his own guilt, doesn't
he?

626
00:31:44,784 --> 00:31:49,973
But while we were still sinners, still
sinning and offending God, God actually

627
00:31:50,003 --> 00:31:53,519
prepared His Son for us, prepared this
Savior for us,

628
00:31:53,549 --> 00:31:58,938
and when the Lord died for us in this way,
while we were still sinners — you see,

629
00:31:58,968 --> 00:32:00,878
this is the very love of God.

630
00:32:00,908 --> 00:32:02,083
This picture tells

631
00:32:02,113 --> 00:32:02,618
a truth,

632
00:32:02,648 --> 00:32:05,963
the very situation that so many people
face today.

633
00:32:05,993 --> 00:32:08,439
A moment ago you said God is so real,

634
00:32:08,469 --> 00:32:09,308
and so good —

635
00:32:09,338 --> 00:32:10,914
so why can't I feel Him?

636
00:32:10,944 --> 00:32:12,721
Why can't I experience Him?

637
00:32:12,751 --> 00:32:15,999
It turns out there is a wall between God
and man,

638
00:32:16,029 --> 00:32:19,144
a very thick wall. And what does the Bible
say?

639
00:32:19,174 --> 00:32:19,679
Our sins

640
00:32:19,709 --> 00:32:21,485
have separated us from God.

641
00:32:21,515 --> 00:32:24,964
Not merely separated us — but cut us off
completely.

642
00:32:24,994 --> 00:32:27,172
And this wall is the wall of sin.

643
00:32:27,202 --> 00:32:28,109
You might say,

644
00:32:28,139 --> 00:32:30,584
but I've never murdered or set fires,

645
00:32:30,614 --> 00:32:32,659
I've never robbed or plundered.

646
00:32:32,689 --> 00:32:36,539
Murder, arson, robbery, and plunder are
the worst of all —

647
00:32:36,569 --> 00:32:38,881
but what does the Bible say sin is?

648
00:32:38,911 --> 00:32:42,561
It is anything at all that goes against
the conscience.

649
00:32:42,591 --> 00:32:44,635
You clearly know what is right,

650
00:32:44,665 --> 00:32:46,240
and yet you don't do it;

651
00:32:46,270 --> 00:32:48,314
you clearly know what is wrong,

652
00:32:48,344 --> 00:32:50,857
and yet you go ahead and do it anyway.

653
00:32:50,887 --> 00:32:52,195
These are your sins.

654
00:32:52,225 --> 00:32:55,875
So it's a fascinating thing — people have
a conscience.

655
00:32:55,905 --> 00:32:58,083
You don't need to raise your hand

656
00:32:58,113 --> 00:33:04,037
during an exam and ask the teacher, "Is it
wrong for me to cheat?" You don't need to
ask.

657
00:33:04,067 --> 00:33:07,383
It isn't something you ever learned out of
a book.

658
00:33:07,413 --> 00:33:11,531
At home you don't need to raise your hand
and ask your mother,

659
00:33:11,561 --> 00:33:17,426
"Mom, is it wrong for me to steal your
money?" You don't need to ask — you
already know.

660
00:33:17,456 --> 00:33:20,863
Anything that goes against the conscience
is sin.

661
00:33:20,893 --> 00:33:26,263
And the most terrible thing about sin is
this: you cannot take it back again.

662
00:33:26,293 --> 00:33:29,139
You tell a lie to deceive someone — fine;

663
00:33:29,169 --> 00:33:35,592
but when you find out that someone has
lied to deceive you, oh, your temper
flares right up.

664
00:33:35,622 --> 00:33:36,714
Some people say,

665
00:33:36,744 --> 00:33:40,221
a man who isn't a bit of a rogue wastes
his youth;

666
00:33:40,251 --> 00:33:44,078
having a mistress is quite an ordinary
thing, they say.

667
00:33:44,108 --> 00:33:46,323
But if his wife were to tell him

668
00:33:46,353 --> 00:33:51,022
that she too had a lover on the side — oh,
it might really be that,

669
00:33:51,052 --> 00:33:52,705
it might really be that,

670
00:33:52,735 --> 00:33:55,300
there's no telling what would happen.

671
00:33:55,330 --> 00:33:57,685
So you find that the terror of sin

672
00:33:57,715 --> 00:34:00,420
is that it goes against the conscience.

673
00:34:00,450 --> 00:34:05,821
The terror of sin is its
self-centeredness, and that you cannot
take it back.

674
00:34:05,851 --> 00:34:12,344
Sin is like a heavy burden pressing down
upon a person; and that chain below — do
you see it?

675
00:34:12,374 --> 00:34:14,869
I believe everyone wants to be good.

676
00:34:14,899 --> 00:34:17,464
I once met a man who cursed terribly.

677
00:34:17,494 --> 00:34:19,007
He resolved to change,

678
00:34:19,037 --> 00:34:22,093
and for a day, then two days, he managed
it;

679
00:34:22,123 --> 00:34:24,057
but when the third day came,

680
00:34:24,087 --> 00:34:27,634
he cursed again, and even worse than he
had before.

681
00:34:27,664 --> 00:34:32,964
I believe everyone wants to be good, but
to sin is to become a slave to sin,

682
00:34:32,994 --> 00:34:34,577
unable ever to be free.

683
00:34:34,607 --> 00:34:36,822
And to sin brings death as well.

684
00:34:36,852 --> 00:34:39,838
Some illnesses today are brought on by
sin,

685
00:34:39,868 --> 00:34:42,503
and some deaths are brought on by sin.

686
00:34:42,533 --> 00:34:48,050
And death is not the end of it; after
death, one must face the judgment of God.

687
00:34:48,080 --> 00:34:50,678
All who sin, God will cast into hell.

688
00:34:50,708 --> 00:34:54,441
If God could make a sun that burns for so
many years,

689
00:34:54,471 --> 00:34:57,140
then of course He is also able to make

690
00:34:57,170 --> 00:35:02,040
a hell, a lake of fire that is never
quenched, into which all who sin

691
00:35:02,070 --> 00:35:02,963
will be cast.

692
00:35:02,993 --> 00:35:06,230
When the Lord Jesus came, at His first
coming,

693
00:35:06,260 --> 00:35:08,218
it was to deal with our sin.

694
00:35:08,248 --> 00:35:08,928
And so, in

695
00:35:08,958 --> 00:35:10,562
the seventh century BC,

696
00:35:10,592 --> 00:35:14,183
seven hundred years before the Lord Jesus
was born,

697
00:35:14,213 --> 00:35:17,308
in the book of Isaiah there are these
words.

698
00:35:17,338 --> 00:35:18,799
It says: just as many

699
00:35:18,829 --> 00:35:20,504
were astonished at Him —

700
00:35:20,534 --> 00:35:21,356
astonished —

701
00:35:21,386 --> 00:35:24,623
His visage was marred more than any other
man,

702
00:35:24,653 --> 00:35:25,475
and His form

703
00:35:25,505 --> 00:35:27,321
more than the sons of men;

704
00:35:27,351 --> 00:35:27,534
so,

705
00:35:27,564 --> 00:35:29,736
He shall sprinkle many nations;

706
00:35:29,766 --> 00:35:32,363
kings shall shut their mouths at Him.

707
00:35:32,393 --> 00:35:34,565
This speaks of one who suffers.

708
00:35:34,595 --> 00:35:36,269
And who exactly is this?

709
00:35:36,299 --> 00:35:42,873
When people saw Him they were astonished —
"astonishing," truly alarmed. And why?
Because His

710
00:35:42,903 --> 00:35:44,862
face was so terribly marred.

711
00:35:44,892 --> 00:35:48,839
In fact, this is speaking of the Lord
Jesus' final days.

712
00:35:48,869 --> 00:35:50,685
After the Lord was seized,

713
00:35:50,715 --> 00:35:53,668
He was dragged away all through the night,

714
00:35:53,698 --> 00:35:55,869
tried in five different places,

715
00:35:55,899 --> 00:36:00,840
because they were set on condemning the
Lord to death before daybreak,

716
00:36:00,870 --> 00:36:02,260
to do away with Him.

717
00:36:02,290 --> 00:36:04,675
So all night long He had no sleep,

718
00:36:04,705 --> 00:36:08,723
passing through trial after trial, torment
after torment.

719
00:36:08,753 --> 00:36:12,629
And then, "His form more marred than the
sons of men" —

720
00:36:12,659 --> 00:36:16,534
what this means is His body, His form, His
very "form,"

721
00:36:16,564 --> 00:36:17,244
was abused

722
00:36:17,274 --> 00:36:24,630
and beaten until it was not like a man's —
more than a man — meaning His appearance,
at a single glance,

723
00:36:24,660 --> 00:36:27,122
no longer looked like a man at all.

724
00:36:27,152 --> 00:36:28,987
And what exactly happened?

725
00:36:29,017 --> 00:36:31,570
That day was, in fact, the Passover.

726
00:36:31,600 --> 00:36:37,095
The governor at the time was Pilate; the
Jews dragged the Lord before Pilate,

727
00:36:37,125 --> 00:36:42,261
and Pilate interrogated the Lord, but
could find no fault in Him at all.

728
00:36:42,291 --> 00:36:46,853
So once, twice, three times he said, I can
find no fault in Him.

729
00:36:46,883 --> 00:36:49,364
What do you want me to do with Him?

730
00:36:49,394 --> 00:36:51,660
Then Pilate thought of a method.

731
00:36:51,690 --> 00:36:54,099
At the Passover there was a custom

732
00:36:54,129 --> 00:36:56,610
that he could release one prisoner.

733
00:36:56,640 --> 00:37:00,198
And he knew the Jews had seized Jesus out
of envy,

734
00:37:00,228 --> 00:37:03,928
not because Jesus had done anything worthy
of death.

735
00:37:03,958 --> 00:37:08,592
So he thought of a method: he had Jesus
scourged by the soldiers.

736
00:37:08,622 --> 00:37:11,964
Those whips were called the
cat-o'-nine-tails —

737
00:37:11,994 --> 00:37:16,126
a single whip splitting into nine, with
metal on the tips.

738
00:37:16,156 --> 00:37:19,713
When it struck, it would sink deep into
the flesh.

739
00:37:19,743 --> 00:37:26,601
There were records of some who, after such
a beating, didn't even need to be
crucified. And why?

740
00:37:26,631 --> 00:37:30,260
you could even see the intestines, because
the back

741
00:37:30,290 --> 00:37:32,125
has so little flesh on it.

742
00:37:32,155 --> 00:37:34,995
And what was the purpose of beating Him?

743
00:37:35,025 --> 00:37:37,578
It was to win the people's sympathy.

744
00:37:37,608 --> 00:37:42,672
So the Bible mentions again and again that
the Lord Jesus was scourged,

745
00:37:42,702 --> 00:37:44,538
and all the more severely.

746
00:37:44,568 --> 00:37:46,260
He had committed no sin,

747
00:37:46,290 --> 00:37:48,986
yet people treated Him as a criminal —

748
00:37:49,016 --> 00:37:54,439
and even so, He did not receive even the
treatment a criminal ought to have,

749
00:37:54,469 --> 00:37:57,746
for He had to be beaten all the more
severely.

750
00:37:57,776 --> 00:38:03,597
After the beating, Pilate brought the Lord
Jesus out and said, "Behold the man!"

751
00:38:03,627 --> 00:38:04,841
And at that time,

752
00:38:04,871 --> 00:38:10,473
the Lord's form was marred more than the
sons of men — that is what it means.

753
00:38:10,503 --> 00:38:12,813
Do you still remember that lamb?

754
00:38:12,843 --> 00:38:15,154
It could not be boiled in water;

755
00:38:15,184 --> 00:38:18,372
the whole of it had to be roasted with
fire.

756
00:38:18,402 --> 00:38:24,077
This shows all the pain, all the torment,
that the Lord passed through for us.

757
00:38:24,107 --> 00:38:25,320
And in the Bible,

758
00:38:25,350 --> 00:38:28,392
in the Psalms there is a saying like this.

759
00:38:28,422 --> 00:38:30,367
What does it say? It says —

760
00:38:30,397 --> 00:38:30,952
it says,

761
00:38:30,982 --> 00:38:31,610
my back —

762
00:38:31,640 --> 00:38:33,146
as if it were a plow,

763
00:38:33,176 --> 00:38:38,778
plowing upon my back, just like a man
plowing a field, plowing upon the back,

764
00:38:38,808 --> 00:38:41,923
and the furrows they plowed were very
long.

765
00:38:41,953 --> 00:38:45,288
I believe this is speaking of this very
thing.

766
00:38:45,318 --> 00:38:47,263
So after Isaiah chapter 52,

767
00:38:47,293 --> 00:38:49,311
there is a saying like this.

768
00:38:49,341 --> 00:38:50,554
What does it say?

769
00:38:50,584 --> 00:38:52,383
It says: who has believed

770
00:38:52,413 --> 00:38:53,187
our report?

771
00:38:53,217 --> 00:38:54,943
And the arm of the LORD,

772
00:38:54,973 --> 00:38:57,064
to whom has it been revealed?

773
00:38:57,094 --> 00:39:01,525
The Lord Jesus, in the identity of a King,
entered Jerusalem;

774
00:39:01,555 --> 00:39:07,450
who could ever have imagined that a few
days later He would come to such a state?

775
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:11,473
So there is a saying below — earlier it
said that kings

776
00:39:11,503 --> 00:39:13,740
would shut their mouths at Him,

777
00:39:13,770 --> 00:39:16,666
because never before had a king, for his

778
00:39:16,696 --> 00:39:17,178
people,

779
00:39:17,208 --> 00:39:18,714
come to such a state.

780
00:39:18,744 --> 00:39:19,226
But He,

781
00:39:19,256 --> 00:39:21,932
His form marred, His face so haggard,

782
00:39:21,962 --> 00:39:24,053
He washed many nations clean.

783
00:39:24,083 --> 00:39:26,832
And this, too, is the arm of the LORD.

784
00:39:26,862 --> 00:39:31,513
It turns out that God stretched out His
arm to save us from sin,

785
00:39:31,543 --> 00:39:34,002
to lift us up out of the miry pit.

786
00:39:34,032 --> 00:39:41,070
And it turns out the word "arm" is the
very same word as the shank bone of the
Passover lamb —

787
00:39:41,100 --> 00:39:42,649
that is, His own arm.

788
00:39:42,679 --> 00:39:44,002
After the beating,

789
00:39:44,032 --> 00:39:47,526
Pilate thought those people would stop
there —

790
00:39:47,556 --> 00:39:49,594
I can find no fault in Him,

791
00:39:49,624 --> 00:39:52,198
yet I've had Him beaten like this.

792
00:39:52,228 --> 00:39:53,476
"Behold the man!"

793
00:39:53,506 --> 00:39:55,356
But what did the Jews do?

794
00:39:55,386 --> 00:39:56,108
They said,

795
00:39:56,138 --> 00:39:57,085
"Crucify Him!

796
00:39:57,115 --> 00:39:58,063
Crucify Him!"

797
00:39:58,093 --> 00:40:00,394
They would rather have a robber

798
00:40:00,424 --> 00:40:01,597
than have Jesus.

799
00:40:01,627 --> 00:40:05,206
And the more they cried out, the louder it
grew.

800
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:08,514
Pilate, seeing there was nothing to be
done,

801
00:40:08,544 --> 00:40:09,792
handed Jesus over

802
00:40:09,822 --> 00:40:12,199
to the soldiers to be crucified.

803
00:40:12,229 --> 00:40:14,003
And what is crucifixion?

804
00:40:14,033 --> 00:40:16,484
A nail as thick as a silver coin,

805
00:40:16,514 --> 00:40:18,214
some nine inches long —

806
00:40:18,244 --> 00:40:21,221
three nails driven through the two hands

807
00:40:21,251 --> 00:40:22,500
and the two feet,

808
00:40:22,530 --> 00:40:25,357
hanging a man of over a hundred pounds

809
00:40:25,387 --> 00:40:26,409
upon the wood.

810
00:40:26,439 --> 00:40:30,094
It is, in fact, a most cruel punishment.
And why?

811
00:40:30,124 --> 00:40:33,252
Because crucifixion does not kill at once.

812
00:40:33,282 --> 00:40:35,056
The blood keeps flowing,

813
00:40:35,086 --> 00:40:39,267
and as He is nailed there, His weight
pulls Him forward.

814
00:40:39,297 --> 00:40:42,951
And you know, when your weight pulls you
forward,

815
00:40:42,981 --> 00:40:44,681
you cannot draw breath.

816
00:40:44,711 --> 00:40:50,395
So in order to breathe, you have to push
yourself up with all your strength;

817
00:40:50,425 --> 00:40:52,651
and when you push yourself up,

818
00:40:52,681 --> 00:40:55,358
your back, already beaten to shreds,

819
00:40:55,388 --> 00:41:00,846
that raw, shredded back is dragged up
against the wood full of splinters,

820
00:41:00,876 --> 00:41:02,719
and with every movement,

821
00:41:02,749 --> 00:41:03,577
the wounds,

822
00:41:03,607 --> 00:41:05,606
the wounds from the nails,

823
00:41:05,636 --> 00:41:07,791
are pulled wider and longer,

824
00:41:07,821 --> 00:41:09,147
wider and longer.

825
00:41:11,568 --> 00:41:15,502
In fact, on the cross, you could say that
every breath,

826
00:41:15,532 --> 00:41:16,872
every gasp for air,

827
00:41:16,902 --> 00:41:17,521
is agony.

828
00:41:17,551 --> 00:41:19,034
And in this very way,

829
00:41:19,064 --> 00:41:22,566
the Lord Jesus, from nine o'clock in the
morning,

830
00:41:22,596 --> 00:41:26,314
hung there all the way until three in the
afternoon.

831
00:41:26,344 --> 00:41:27,251
Now by rights

832
00:41:27,281 --> 00:41:30,495
it should have been daytime, bright with
sun;

833
00:41:30,525 --> 00:41:33,883
but at twelve noon, the whole land turned
dark.

834
00:41:33,913 --> 00:41:35,036
It was as if God

835
00:41:35,066 --> 00:41:38,208
wanted people to take notice of this thing
—

836
00:41:38,238 --> 00:41:41,812
to look upon this Savior crucified upon
the cross.

837
00:41:41,842 --> 00:41:46,497
The whole land turning dark is, of course,
deeply meaningful too.

838
00:41:46,527 --> 00:41:49,164
For the sun represents righteousness;

839
00:41:49,194 --> 00:41:56,011
yet at that very moment, when there was no
righteousness at all, the One least
deserving to die

840
00:41:56,041 --> 00:41:57,886
was the very One who died.

841
00:41:57,916 --> 00:42:01,922
And when He had hung there until three in
the afternoon,

842
00:42:01,952 --> 00:42:04,589
the Lord cried out with a loud voice:

843
00:42:04,619 --> 00:42:07,688
"My God, My God, why have You forsaken
Me?"

844
00:42:07,718 --> 00:42:12,950
It turns out that in that moment, it was
not only the agony of the cross;

845
00:42:12,980 --> 00:42:15,617
the Father too stretched out His hand

846
00:42:15,647 --> 00:42:16,626
to strike Him,

847
00:42:16,656 --> 00:42:18,212
to punish His own Son.

848
00:42:18,242 --> 00:42:18,789
And then

849
00:42:18,819 --> 00:42:21,456
the Lord cried out with a loud voice,

850
00:42:21,486 --> 00:42:23,618
and He said, "It is finished."

851
00:42:23,648 --> 00:42:25,204
Then He bowed His head

852
00:42:25,234 --> 00:42:27,511
and committed His spirit to God.

853
00:42:27,541 --> 00:42:31,042
And at that time it was just past three
o'clock —

854
00:42:31,072 --> 00:42:34,430
the very time for the slaughtering of the
lamb,

855
00:42:34,460 --> 00:42:36,665
the very time of the Passover —

856
00:42:36,695 --> 00:42:38,250
representing the Lord,

857
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,836
for us upon the cross,

858
00:42:39,866 --> 00:42:42,143
at the very moment of His death.

859
00:42:42,173 --> 00:42:46,257
The Chinese charac
ter 來, "to come," 
is deeply meaningf
ul.

860
00:42:46,287 --> 00:42:50,220
The character 來 ha
s a cross right in
 the middle of it.

861
00:42:50,250 --> 00:42:51,615
And then all people

862
00:42:51,645 --> 00:42:54,477
ought to come to the foot of the cross.

863
00:42:54,507 --> 00:42:59,615
And so, going on from here, I would like
to share a hymn with you all.

864
00:42:59,645 --> 00:43:01,156
The name of this hymn

865
00:43:01,186 --> 00:43:02,844
is "Come, Please Feel."

866
00:43:02,874 --> 00:43:06,074
Let us go together to the foot of the
cross,

867
00:43:06,104 --> 00:43:10,331
and see this Jesus, and all that He passed
through for us.

868
00:43:10,361 --> 00:43:12,753
All that He passed through for us

869
00:43:12,783 --> 00:43:14,220
was not for Himself,

870
00:43:14,250 --> 00:43:15,450
but was for us.

871
00:43:37,200 --> 00:43:39,926
God's love is

872
00:43:39,956 --> 00:43:45,225
displayed upon the cross;

873
00:43:45,255 --> 00:43:48,240
for me the Lord

874
00:43:48,270 --> 00:43:53,466
endured torment and scorn,

875
00:43:53,496 --> 00:44:01,196
shamed by men,

876
00:44:01,226 --> 00:44:06,884
heaped with slander.

877
00:44:06,914 --> 00:44:08,107
The Father's beloved Son tasted

878
00:44:08,137 --> 00:44:12,330
every mockery and torment,

879
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:18,488
crowned with thorns,

880
00:44:20,518 --> 00:44:23,936
and cruelly scourged,

881
00:44:23,966 --> 00:44:25,001
His body covered

882
00:44:25,031 --> 00:44:30,382
over with wounds.

883
00:44:32,412 --> 00:44:36,540
Hands and feet nailed fast,

884
00:44:37,570 --> 00:44:41,989
hung high upon the wood,

885
00:44:42,019 --> 00:44:44,632
in utter agony —

886
00:44:44,662 --> 00:44:49,465
who can feel it?

887
00:45:29,232 --> 00:45:30,909
The pain

888
00:45:30,939 --> 00:45:32,999
that never ceases.

889
00:45:33,029 --> 00:45:36,105
His face gaunt and wasted,

890
00:45:38,135 --> 00:45:40,284
hung on the cross,

891
00:45:40,314 --> 00:45:45,229
His bones now all laid bare,

892
00:45:47,259 --> 00:45:48,648
blood streaming

893
00:45:49,678 --> 00:45:51,772
down His face,

894
00:45:52,802 --> 00:45:56,157
dripping to the ground,

895
00:45:57,187 --> 00:45:59,896
sorely wounded,

896
00:46:00,926 --> 00:46:01,979
yet struck even

897
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:04,789
by the Father.

898
00:46:06,819 --> 00:46:10,742
Who could write a poem

899
00:46:11,772 --> 00:46:15,932
to capture such love?

900
00:46:16,962 --> 00:46:17,781
His love,

901
00:46:17,811 --> 00:46:23,842
engraved within my heart.

902
00:46:24,872 --> 00:46:29,743
How fresh His mercy,

903
00:46:30,773 --> 00:46:33,869
deep and wide —

904
00:46:33,899 --> 00:46:35,511
the grace of the cross,

905
00:46:36,541 --> 00:46:41,315
who can ever fathom it?

906
00:46:43,345 --> 00:46:45,957
My Lord even

907
00:46:45,987 --> 00:46:51,761
cried out, "It is finished."

908
00:46:53,791 --> 00:46:55,939
I will ponder it

909
00:46:55,969 --> 00:47:00,207
ten thousand times over.

910
00:47:02,237 --> 00:47:06,365
Jesus, my Lord,

911
00:47:06,395 --> 00:47:10,813
Your love runs deep and will never die.

912
00:47:11,843 --> 00:47:13,456
This grace

913
00:47:13,486 --> 00:47:19,259
forever moves us.

914
00:47:20,289 --> 00:47:22,573
This deep grace —

915
00:47:22,603 --> 00:47:23,431
come,

916
00:47:23,461 --> 00:47:31,900
and feel it.

917
00:48:07,311 --> 00:48:09,615
At the very end of the hymn there is a line —

918
00:48:10,127 --> 00:48:11,121
from the Bible.

919
00:48:11,151 --> 00:48:12,687
It says: He loved me

920
00:48:13,455 --> 00:48:14,655
and gave Himself for me.

921
00:48:15,759 --> 00:48:18,063
It turns out this Anointed One was cut off,

922
00:48:18,575 --> 00:48:19,775
having nothing —

923
00:48:21,391 --> 00:48:22,591
not for Himself.

924
00:48:24,207 --> 00:48:25,201
He is the One who

925
00:48:25,231 --> 00:48:26,511
loved me and gave Himself for me.

926
00:48:30,863 --> 00:48:34,703
It turns out that God used a method like this to save you and me.

927
00:48:36,240 --> 00:48:39,311
The Bible says it like this: when we,

928
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:41,103
like sheep, had gone astray,

929
00:48:42,127 --> 00:48:43,377
each one turning to his own way,

930
00:48:43,407 --> 00:48:46,705
it says that the LORD —

931
00:48:46,735 --> 00:48:47,490
that is, the Father —

932
00:48:47,520 --> 00:48:51,343
would lay the iniquity of us all upon Him,

933
00:48:51,400 --> 00:48:53,873
upon the Son, the Lord Jesus.

934
00:48:53,903 --> 00:48:58,880
This is what Isaiah chapter 53 goes on to say.

935
00:49:00,047 --> 00:49:02,863
God used this method, the method of substitution.

936
00:49:03,360 --> 00:49:05,423
He died for us

937
00:49:05,935 --> 00:49:07,135
so that today we

938
00:49:07,215 --> 00:49:07,953
could

939
00:49:07,983 --> 00:49:10,513
have our sins forgiven.

940
00:49:10,543 --> 00:49:13,615
He died for us so that today we could have life.

941
00:49:16,431 --> 00:49:18,223
So the Chinese character for "righteousness" —

942
00:49:18,735 --> 00:49:20,271
how is it written? It is a lamb

943
00:49:21,039 --> 00:49:22,239
placed over "me."

944
00:49:23,087 --> 00:49:25,391
It turns out the Lord Jesus died in my place.

945
00:49:26,159 --> 00:49:27,951
He is the Passover lamb.

946
00:49:29,743 --> 00:49:33,041
And when He died in my place, for me, today I can be justified.

947
00:49:33,071 --> 00:49:36,397
My sin is fully dealt with; I have sin no more.

948
00:49:36,655 --> 00:49:38,447
And I am able to know

949
00:49:38,703 --> 00:49:39,983
and enjoy a free, abundant life,

950
00:49:40,495 --> 00:49:41,489
to know

951
00:49:41,519 --> 00:49:43,055
what is beautiful and what is good.

952
00:49:46,639 --> 00:49:51,886
How precious — after the Lord died, on the
third day He rose again from the dead.

953
00:49:51,916 --> 00:49:54,231
In fact, that year was very special,

954
00:49:54,261 --> 00:49:55,599
because that year the

955
00:49:55,629 --> 00:49:56,120
Passover

956
00:49:56,150 --> 00:49:57,227
fell on a Friday.

957
00:49:57,257 --> 00:49:59,377
So after the Lord died, next came

958
00:49:59,407 --> 00:50:01,412
the Feast of Unleavened Bread —

959
00:50:01,442 --> 00:50:07,846
and in fact the Feast of Unleavened Bread
means that the effect of the Lord's death
was immediate.

960
00:50:07,876 --> 00:50:09,865
That is, He dealt with our sin.

961
00:50:09,895 --> 00:50:12,471
Then, after the Sabbath, after Saturday,

962
00:50:12,501 --> 00:50:13,579
on the third day,

963
00:50:13,609 --> 00:50:16,640
the first day of the week, the Lord rose
again,

964
00:50:16,670 --> 00:50:21,396
fulfilling the Lord's own word that He
would rise again after three days.

965
00:50:21,426 --> 00:50:22,894
Do you remember we said

966
00:50:22,924 --> 00:50:27,454
that the Feast of Firstfruits is not
necessarily three days afterward?

967
00:50:27,484 --> 00:50:29,343
But that year was so special:

968
00:50:29,373 --> 00:50:33,187
the Feast of Firstfruits, the third day
after the Passover.

969
00:50:33,217 --> 00:50:37,747
The Feast of Firstfruits shows that the
Lord Jesus is the firstfruits.

970
00:50:37,777 --> 00:50:40,743
He was the first to rise from the dead for
us.

971
00:50:40,773 --> 00:50:45,629
And the Bible also says that just as He
rose, so one day we too shall rise.

972
00:50:45,659 --> 00:50:48,430
The Lord's resurrection declares one
thing:

973
00:50:48,460 --> 00:50:50,971
that He has already dealt with our sin.

974
00:50:51,001 --> 00:50:54,684
For if He had not dealt with it, He could
not have risen,

975
00:50:54,714 --> 00:50:56,899
because the wages of sin is death.

976
00:50:56,929 --> 00:51:02,827
But the Lord's resurrection lets us know
that this salvation has already been
accomplished.

977
00:51:02,857 --> 00:51:03,218
Today,

978
00:51:03,248 --> 00:51:04,130
anyone at all,

979
00:51:04,160 --> 00:51:08,430
as long as he is willing to receive the
Lord Jesus as his Savior —

980
00:51:08,460 --> 00:51:10,254
the Lord is able to help him

981
00:51:10,284 --> 00:51:11,100
overcome sin.

982
00:51:11,130 --> 00:51:13,837
Is that not "to finish the transgression"?

983
00:51:13,867 --> 00:51:17,489
He is also able to forgive the sins of a
whole lifetime.

984
00:51:17,519 --> 00:51:21,130
Is that not "to make reconciliation for
iniquity"?

985
00:51:21,160 --> 00:51:23,241
He will do away with our sin.

986
00:51:23,271 --> 00:51:25,863
The Lord came for this very purpose.

987
00:51:25,893 --> 00:51:29,067
And once sin is dealt with, there is no
more

988
00:51:29,097 --> 00:51:31,033
wall of sin to separate us.

989
00:51:31,063 --> 00:51:34,819
Do you see the pair of hands that God
stretches out?

990
00:51:34,849 --> 00:51:37,659
He wants to gather us into His embrace.

991
00:51:37,689 --> 00:51:39,188
We can cast ourselves

992
00:51:39,218 --> 00:51:42,611
into the welcoming arms of God, into the
loving

993
00:51:42,641 --> 00:51:43,703
embrace of God.

994
00:51:43,733 --> 00:51:47,708
And God gives us the richest and very best
preparation,

995
00:51:47,738 --> 00:51:52,878
so that we can receive every spiritual
blessing in the heavenly places.

996
00:51:52,908 --> 00:51:54,480
Our sins are forgiven,

997
00:51:54,510 --> 00:51:58,121
and we can have true love, and true peace
and joy.

998
00:51:58,151 --> 00:52:02,271
We are reconciled to God, shaking hands
and making peace,

999
00:52:02,301 --> 00:52:04,237
beginning an abundant life,

1000
00:52:04,267 --> 00:52:09,626
able to become the children of God, with a
bright and warm home in heaven.

1001
00:52:09,656 --> 00:52:10,499
And one day,

1002
00:52:10,529 --> 00:52:14,359
the Lord will come again to take us there
to Himself.

1003
00:52:14,389 --> 00:52:15,232
Where He is,

1004
00:52:15,262 --> 00:52:16,834
there we too shall be.

1005
00:52:16,864 --> 00:52:20,621
So you see that the Lord is the bright
morning star.

1006
00:52:20,651 --> 00:52:25,354
And having come to this point, I would
like to take a little time

1007
00:52:25,384 --> 00:52:30,524
for any friend here at our gathering today
who, if you do not yet know,

1008
00:52:30,554 --> 00:52:34,893
if you have not yet received the Lord
Jesus as your Savior —

1009
00:52:34,923 --> 00:52:36,859
you can make this decision.

1010
00:52:36,889 --> 00:52:39,116
You can pray to the Lord Jesus.

1011
00:52:39,146 --> 00:52:41,082
You may pray in your heart,

1012
00:52:41,112 --> 00:52:43,267
or you may pray softly aloud —

1013
00:52:43,297 --> 00:52:45,014
and the meaning is this:

1014
00:52:45,044 --> 00:52:45,815
Lord Jesus,

1015
00:52:45,845 --> 00:52:47,490
I am willing to repent,

1016
00:52:47,520 --> 00:52:48,881
and to sin no more.

1017
00:52:48,911 --> 00:52:52,699
I ask You to forgive all the sins of my
whole life.

1018
00:52:52,729 --> 00:52:56,742
I am willing to receive You as my own
personal Savior.

1019
00:52:56,772 --> 00:52:58,015
A sincere prayer.

1020
00:52:58,045 --> 00:53:02,057
And when you pray like this, God is deeply
responsive.

1021
00:53:02,087 --> 00:53:03,480
When Daniel prayed,

1022
00:53:03,510 --> 00:53:05,875
God gave him the seventy sevens.

1023
00:53:05,905 --> 00:53:08,720
God is deeply responsive, and when you

1024
00:53:08,750 --> 00:53:16,431
pray to the Lord in true sincerity like
this — the Lord came to bear your sin, and
to forgive your sin.

1025
00:53:16,461 --> 00:53:19,800
He died upon the cross for this very
purpose.

1026
00:53:19,830 --> 00:53:25,340
He will surely forgive your sin, and
cleanse you from all unrighteousness.

1027
00:53:25,370 --> 00:53:27,212
Let us take a little time

1028
00:53:27,242 --> 00:53:29,084
for any friend here today

1029
00:53:29,114 --> 00:53:33,351
who has not yet received the Lord, to make
this decision.

1030
00:53:33,381 --> 00:53:37,394
If you are willing to receive the Lord as
your Savior,

1031
00:53:37,424 --> 00:53:39,714
you can pray with me like this.

1032
00:53:39,744 --> 00:53:40,912
I'll say a line,

1033
00:53:40,942 --> 00:53:43,008
and you say a line after me;

1034
00:53:43,038 --> 00:53:45,778
or you may simply pray in your heart.

1035
00:53:45,808 --> 00:53:46,976
Do not hesitate.

1036
00:53:47,006 --> 00:53:51,318
The people around you long for you to
believe in the Lord.

1037
00:53:51,348 --> 00:53:54,313
God has prepared this salvation for you.

1038
00:53:54,343 --> 00:53:57,832
If today you are willing to receive the
Lord as

1039
00:53:57,862 --> 00:53:58,730
your Savior,

1040
00:53:58,760 --> 00:54:00,452
you can pray like this.

1041
00:54:00,482 --> 00:54:01,425
Let us begin.

1042
00:54:01,455 --> 00:54:02,249
Lord Jesus,

1043
00:54:02,279 --> 00:54:03,971
I am willing to repent,

1044
00:54:04,001 --> 00:54:05,393
and to sin no more.

1045
00:54:05,423 --> 00:54:09,211
I ask You to forgive all the sins of my
whole life.

1046
00:54:09,241 --> 00:54:13,254
I am willing to receive You as my own
personal Savior.

1047
00:54:13,284 --> 00:54:14,557
A sincere prayer.

1048
00:54:23,631 --> 00:54:28,531
If you prayed along just now with that
prayer, congratulations to you.

1049
00:54:28,561 --> 00:54:35,925
And you can tell the friend who invited
you to our gathering today, "I have come
to believe in the Lord."

1050
00:54:35,955 --> 00:54:38,108
In fact, the Feasts of the LORD

1051
00:54:38,138 --> 00:54:40,573
could be called God's own calendar.

1052
00:54:40,603 --> 00:54:42,474
At the Lord's first coming,

1053
00:54:42,504 --> 00:54:44,234
He was the Passover lamb.

1054
00:54:44,264 --> 00:54:45,784
He dealt with our sin.

1055
00:54:45,814 --> 00:54:48,671
Then came the Feast of Unleavened Bread —

1056
00:54:48,701 --> 00:54:51,417
His salvation is powerful and complete.

1057
00:54:51,447 --> 00:54:53,178
And He rose again for us.

1058
00:54:53,208 --> 00:54:58,319
How precious — then the Holy Spirit came,
and the family of God appeared.

1059
00:54:58,349 --> 00:55:03,389
Just as the Lord, at His first coming,
fulfilled the words of the Bible,

1060
00:55:03,419 --> 00:55:08,459
in the same way you'll find that the Lord
Jesus will come a second time.

1061
00:55:08,489 --> 00:55:13,882
He will come back to receive all who
believe in Him, to take them to Himself,

1062
00:55:13,912 --> 00:55:17,333
and He has, for us, prepared a glorious
eternity.

1063
00:55:17,363 --> 00:55:19,093
May the days ahead of you

1064
00:55:19,123 --> 00:55:25,320
bring an ever-deeper experience of the
Lord, and may the Lord's love be with you
always.
